<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jutland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jutland is the peninsula of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> that forms the mainland of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, together with the northern part of the German state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>. Probably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutes">Jutes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a> who migrated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the 5th century, it was a core land of the early Danish kingdom. Its southern part, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a>, was long disputed between Denmark and the German states, and in 1916 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> off its coast saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jutland">Battle of Jutland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jutland.jpg" alt="Jutland" width="320" height="579" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LibIchtnatz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jutland_Peninsula_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
